WEBVTT

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.400
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.390
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.470
Could I have some when they're done?

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:16.990
Just a couple, okay?

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.270
The rest are for our customers.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.290
Got it!

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.550
Raichi, think any girls will give you chocolate?

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.090
You and Onee-chan.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.190
What about girls from school or from around the neighborhood?

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.980
Maybe a girl you haven't talked 
to much will suddenly call you out,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.060
or maybe you'll find some chocolate in your locker {screw the post}

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:48.440
with an unsigned letter that simply says "I love you".

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.010
That really brings back memories...

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.450
This chocolate... is-for-you!

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.950
Nee-san!

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.400
Hi, signalize!

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.680
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.680
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.570
No, that's wrong

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.570
iie chigau yo

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.950
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.950
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.740
Do that signalize!

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.920
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.920
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.880
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.880
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.420
So I'll believe in the present

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.420
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.590
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.590
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.930
Chance for me

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:57.230
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:57.230
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:01.440
It's just another challenge on the way

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:01.440
hora chousen matteru yo

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:06.360
Where are we headed?

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:06.360
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.110
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.110
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:17.370
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:17.370
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.750
Where we're headed

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.750
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.630
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.630
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.970
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.970
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.450
This one's cute!

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.840
Doesn't it look hard to make?

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.040
Oh, chocolate. Do we have cooking classes today?

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.870
No, we're thinking about making these for Valentine's.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.850
Right?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.850
Valentine's...

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.930
They're making chocolate for Valentine's Day.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.360
Why are you whispering?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.830
They're talking about chocolate <i>for</i> Valentine's Day.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.020
Doesn't that mean they have a boy they like?

00:02:59.020 --> 00:02:59.980
Probably.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.740
But isn't romance forbidden for idols?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.450
They might be making it for their friends.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.310
It's exciting thinking about who'll give chocolate to whom.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.790
It's a good chance to update my relationship chart. {wow, Aoi}

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.250
I think it's fine if the feelings are just one-sided.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:16.770
But didn't you say it was absolutely forbidden before?

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.090
I never said "absolutely".

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.630
Ran, no way?!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.140
D-Don't get me wrong!

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.890
Ichigo-chan, Aoi-chan, Ran-chan!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.640
Sensei wants to talk to us!

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.960
A Valentine Fashion Show?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.650
Yeah. An offer came for you honeys.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.920
Does that mean there's no audition?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.360
What kind of event is it?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.640
Simply, it's a Valentine Party for girls in love!

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.510
You'll use lovely and cute date coords to inspire them.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.660
Yeah!

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.910
This is bad.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.290
Yeah.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.670
Why? Aren't you happy we got this gig?

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:00.170
I'm happy about that, but Ichigo— have you ever been in love?

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.670
Nope.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.530
And Otome?

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.680
Love you!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.860
Have you ever given someone chocolate for Valentine's?

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:07.910
Never.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.150
Same here. What about you?

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.100
I've never wanted to.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.100
I've done it, actually.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.060
We give out cookies every year at our shop.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.420
Those <i>aren't</i> chocolate.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.020
<i>That</i>?! {damn Japanese humor}

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.340
Chocolate would just melt if you put it in a bento.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.470
So none of us have any experience?

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.950
Right, and that's the problem.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.080
Most of our guests will be girls in love.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.920
Do you think we can really support those girls when none of us have even given out chocolate before?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.490
Oh, so you're saying that we need to love, right?

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.200
You can't <i>just</i> love, you need to <i>fall</i> in love.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.010
Fall?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.070
Where?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.670
Here!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.970
Yes, Otome?

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.680
Chocolate is filled with love. That's why girls give out chocolate!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.900
I see! So we just need to be the filling!

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.480
Enough already!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.410
So?

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.480
Let's make chocolate together!

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.610
Aha! So we'll figure out how girls in love think by making Valentine chocolate?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.110
Exactly!

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.740
The kitchen's booked through tomorrow.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.870
I guess there are a lot of girls who 
want to make homemade chocolate.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.920
I reserved some space for us the day after tomorrow.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.110
Thanks.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.420
Can we <i>really</i> understand how 
those girls feel just by making chocolate?

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.540
It's much better than not doing anything, right?

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.110
It'll be fun!

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.030
We'll fill them with our sweet, sweet love! {Ok, starting now I'm making Otome extremely lewd}

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.930
I guess I can't complain.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:28.930
Yay!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.810
Let's get to deciding what cards we'll use for the fashion show.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.850
Then we'll meet up at my room tonight.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.810
That one's no good. Do it over.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.500
Wh-What about this?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.070
Oh, so that's what you'd wear to a date? Interesting.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.990
Well, I've never been on a date before...

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.660
Otome hasn't either!

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.870
Right?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.330
Even so, since we've been chosen, we have to be good models for everyone else.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.440
Girls' eyes are unforgiving.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.080
What outfit are you going with, Ran?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.390
Me?

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:08.100
From top to bottom, Black Rider's Jacket, Bold Frilly Mini Skirt,

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.710
and Studded Boots.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.600
Cool, Sexy, and Sexy.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.970
But the card types don't match up...

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:18.790
The important thing this time is to make your coord something you'd wear on a Valentine's Day date.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.540
We're doing Good Coords, right?

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:21.980
Good Coords?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.780
It's a type of combination.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:28.970
Usually, you want to match the Top, Bottom, and Shoes' types,

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.490
but Good Coords are an exception.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.810
It's fine to use all different types.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.910
In exchange, you need to have good sense. {fashion sense, duh}

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:39.000
But if you mess up, it'll <i>really</i> be terrible.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.750
Scary!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.260
That's exactly why we usually avoid them.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.900
But if you're able to pull off an Appeal limited to Good Coords,

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:50.760
then it really makes it worth the risk.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.260
Ran, could you take a look at my coord?

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.520
I just got a great idea! Aoi, take off your shirt. {best line}

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.640
Now stand over there.

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:02.400
Around here?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.110
I get it.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.200
It's the Naughty Detective uniform.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:13.570
White Cyber No-sleeved Top, 
Shiny Black Skirt, and Fur Silver Sandals.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.620
Cool, Sexy, and Sexy.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.220
I call it, "Naughty Detective's Valentine.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.860
The culprit is Y-O-U."

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.240
Culprit apprehended!

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:23.830
Apprehended!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.380
It looks nice, but isn't it a bit too much?

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.970
Really? Maybe I'll change it just a little...

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.890
Here, here! Me too!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.340
So cute!

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.470
It really is!

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:39.590
High Cut Sneakers, White Capri Pants, and Pop'n Candy Shirt.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.780
Cute!

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:42.700
And rare!

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.310
It's certainly good, but whether it has wide appeal or not...

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.980
She's so cute it doesn't matter!

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.570
Too cute...

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:54.310
Aoi-chan, is it alright if I borrow the card you were just using?

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.120
Well?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:58.900
It's great!

00:07:58.900 --> 00:07:59.870
So cool!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.970
Those reel in the Top's sweetness.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.670
It's all thanks to Aoi-chan's card.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.250
Trading cards— I hadn't thought about that.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.230
Now we've all got more to choose from.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.010
That sounds fun!

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.790
We need to choose shoes for Aoi-chan too. Which would work?

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:17.050
Wow, I <i>never</i> get to see Otome-chan's cards.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.560
I wanna see too!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.550
<i>After</i> you pick your own.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:22.640
Understood!

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.540
Thank you very much.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.150
Oh?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.330
That's amazing. So we can watch it from here?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.900
Yeah! It'll be on the net.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:36.500
I'll need to tell Raichi too! I can't wait.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.170
I get to see my daughter's date clothes!

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.360
It was super hard to choose them.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:41.410
There they are!

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.170
Why did you suddenly decide to make chocolate?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:46.670
Because that's where the love is.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.920
Aoi-neesan's making chocolate?!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.560
She said it's to figure out what love is. {what is love?}

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.900
She's so cute.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.710
Wonder if I should head over to help her?

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.670
Sounds fun.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.180
But that's a no-go.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.050
I'm sure they wouldn't let you in even if you did go.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:01.720
Why?

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:06.430
Starlight Academy is a girls' school. Boys aren't allowed in.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.840
Who's Aoi-neesan going to give chocolate to?

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.970
It'd be lame if I asked her over the phone.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.200
If only I was a girl I could check it out...

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.710
You. Where's your uniform?

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.840
Um, being cleaned?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:51.660
Did you see a girl around ten years 
old wearing a pink ribbon walk by?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:52.970
I haven't.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:54.520
Let's try the gym.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.240
Onii-chan, you saved me.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:03.370
Whatever. You're bringing something your sister forgot, right?

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.580
R-Right.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.780
Go straight home when you're done.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:09.440
Okay, and thank you.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.750
Just like his older sister. {Do you think he know's Raichi's a boy?} {He knows everything}

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.260
This is the idol school where idols go to become idols!

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:27.770
What're you doing here?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.020
Hey, stranger girl?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.610
Johnny!

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:37.780
You're the genius who's in charge of making all of Mizuki-sama's choreography!

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.500
You're Johnny Bepp, right?!

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.730
Can't you show me a bit more respect?! {hmm...}

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.540
I wanna get started baking!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.000
Hang in there until after school.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.800
Aoi-neesan! Onee-chan!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.010
Raichi!

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:01.110
Why're you here? And hey, those are <i>my</i> clothes.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.120
You look good in them.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.510
You think so?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.490
Even if she's your sister, non-students aren't allowed here.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.180
Please send her straight home.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.160
Oh, of course—

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.150
"Sister"?!

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:17.440
I'm sorry! I just wanted to see my big sis.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:22.020
She barely ever comes home now that she's enrolled here,

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:25.700
and I was just so lonely without her.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.580
Sorry, cute girl!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.210
Raichi-chan!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.210
What acting...

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.220
This is Starmiya's little sister.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.350
Everyone, get along well with her.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:42.720
Yes.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.350
It's just Raichi...

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:53.850
It's Michiru-sama! And Mr. CoCo's so tiny and adorable!

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.860
Hirari!

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.490
Just for today, alright?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.300
Okay.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.370
Welcome to Starlight Academy.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.090
I get to be Nee-san's classmate...

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.620
<i>No, no!</i>

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.000
The basics of Coordination are to match card types,

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.050
however, it's also possible to mix and match. That is what we call a Good Coord.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.750
<i>I didn't come here to fool around.</i>

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:25.720
<i>I just came to check up on who Aoi-neesan</i>

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.770
<i>will give chocolate... to...</i>

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.520
Amazing! Idols are amazingly awesome!

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.070
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:47.580
You do so many sit-ups and push 
your limits singing and dancing.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.700
You put in so much effort every day.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.550
It's more like we've got no choice 
<i>but </i>to give everything we've got.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.920
That's right. We can only shine <i>because</i>
 of our efforts behind the scenes.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:12:59.900
Raichi, you should get going soon.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.460
I don't wanna...

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.420
Come on!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.330
I wanna help you make chocolate.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.760
Wha— huh? How'd you find out?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.220
Can't I?

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.470
Am I not allowed?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.210
Don't you think it's okay?

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.930
Raichi, do you like chocolate?

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.230
I do! I love it! I can eat it till my stomach bursts!

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:19.880
Don't get too excited. {Not with chocolate but with excitement}

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.440
Here. Love you.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.700
Hey, stop messing around.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.490
Ichigo, who are you giving it to?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.000
Huh? These aren't to eat ourselves?

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.210
I guess we <i>could</i>...

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:42.460
Don't you think it'll be easier to understand the heart of a girl in love if you make them intending to give them out?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.060
I see.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.970
Wonder who I should give it to?

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.900
My family, Aoi, Ran,

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:50.760
Otome-chan, Sensei...

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.350
That's too many!

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:56.520
<i>Who... just who are you making it for? {I guess it's technically whom, but Raichi seems like an ungrammatical kind of guy}</i>

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.010
Otome-chan, that's huge!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.220
Whoever you give that to won't be able to finish it all.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.780
Here I go!

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.330
It's for yourself?!

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.280
It's full of love!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.780
I made them look like strawberries. Aren't they cute?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.820
It's like you're saying, "Please eat me up". {lewd! they're all lewd!} {does anyone actually use the word lewd in real life?}

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.530
What are you saying? {don't know where to emphasize}

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.790
I mixed in cereal with mine.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.290
It's delicious.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.610
Can I have some too?

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.070
Let's taste test!

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:20.290
Not yet.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.060
"Not yet"?

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.800
I'll give them to you... on Valentine's.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.790
Really? They're for us?

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:28.380
It's friendship chocolate?

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:29.800
So it's friendship chocolate.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.480
That's right, got a problem?!

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.960
No, I'm happy!

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:36.180
Same as me. I made friendship chocolate too.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:42.190
Onee-chan, Ran-san, Otome-san... Wh-Who's is this?

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.940
Oh, that one's...

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.700
for my Dad.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.260
Raichi seemed pretty depressed.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:57.830
Really?

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.840
Well then, I'll be leaving now.

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.540
Do you think he wanted chocolate too?

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.680
I wish I'd made some for him.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:12.680
I totally forgot that Raichi's a guy too.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.560
I can't blame you for that. {eh, should actually indicate the clothes reference?}

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:18.350
I can't go giving him my Dad's share either. {I thought Ichigo would give up hers, or that Aoi would do something during the concert later}

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.040
Yeah, I'd feel bad for him then.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.320
Don't worry! He'll get chocolate from mom and me. {Ichigo-mama is Raichi-mama too}

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.610
I'm sure Raichi'll get over it after a good night's rest.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.410
Here, your chocolate. {I guess being cute runs in the family}

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.500
I wanted Aoi-neesan's chocolate...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:39.870
Well aren't <i>you</i> greedy.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.300
Come back home soon after school ends.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.930
We can't watch the Fashion Show online if you're not here.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.140
Yeah...

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:59.260
Hello, everyhoney. {I love this guy}

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.830
It's the day everyone yearns for sweet chocolate.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.050
But I'm a teacher!

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.650
I'm unable to answer your love.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:12.650
But! Obligation chocolate is welcome!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.660
Everyone sure is shy today...

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:24.300
Our special training this time ended 
up being just making chocolate...

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.520
It was really fun!

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.670
I suppose so.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.470
I want to play with Raichi-chan again!

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:38.320
Girls, it's time for the Valentine Fashion Show.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.740
Are you all ready?

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:40.310
Yes!

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:41.890
Want to do a chant?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:42.560
Sure.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.020
What'll it be?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.020
Choco is power, super sweet!

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.070
That seems a bit...

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.440
Choco is power, love love!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.950
That's barely different.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:54.950
Ran?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.470
Something simple...

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:58.160
Like "I Love You"...

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.830
Say something!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.080
We're out of time, let's do it!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.580
Here we go! One, two...

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.580
I love you!

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.830
Will they be alright?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.900
So they <i>did</i> prepare Good Coords.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:52.900
It's starting.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.460
A Good Coord Special Appeal!

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.970
Aoi-chan sure was cute, huh?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.970
Yeah, the cutest.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.310
That's right.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.290
Your show was wonderful!

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:56.720
Please take this!

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:58.870
I don't really like sweet things...

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.490
I kept the sweetness down.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:02.820
Mine's hidden flavor is tabasco.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.330
Good evening, this is Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:06.870
Today is Valentine's Day.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.610
Has you all given your chocolate to someone yet?

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:12.870
I gave some to the people who are always taking care of me...

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:18.880
Handmade?

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.110
Thank you for everything.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:23.330
Is all of that...?

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.900
Ah, excuse me!

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.980
Thank you for everything.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.580
This is your share.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.390
It's chocolate.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:38.380
If I accept this...

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:40.480
will it explode?!

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.280
It will not!

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.530
This...

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.180
It's Valentine chocolate.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.030
Sorry it's a bit late.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:52.960
Thank you.

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:56.500
I'm always getting gifts from you.

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:59.500
{Huh? }Did I give you something before?

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:05.050
Is this your...?

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.740
I went ahead and signed it.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:09.010
"To Raichi".

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:12.140
Amazing! I'll make this my heirloom!

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:15.310
I don't mind that, but be sure to give it a taste too.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:16.620
Of course!

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:18.310
Looks like they're having fun.

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:21.870
Aoi-neesan, I'll always be behind you! {Takamina!!}{Takamina!!}{Did you really need two sets of braces for that?}{Oops, guess it copied over}

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:57.720
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.770
Headmistress, your chocolate was sweet.

00:24:00.770 --> 00:24:02.540
And it didn't explode, right?

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:05.860
Non non, I was so happy that <i>I</i> exploded!

00:24:05.860 --> 00:24:07.390
How dangerous!

00:24:07.930 --> 00:24:09.800
Put your feelings into chocolate!

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:12.060
The moon is really pretty.

00:24:12.060 --> 00:24:15.180
On a night such as this, my blood boils for its prey.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:15.890
Huh?

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:17.010
I found you!

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:17.900
No!

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:19.410
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.410 --> 00:24:21.510
The Moonlit Girl Gives Off a Secret Scent.

00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:23.900
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
